# SEQUENCE  Map  (Thrmnlra)  the redesign from the owner's notes of 13 Nov
# (~/projects/LIB_LLMOUT/Read/LIB_GAMES/Game_Feedback_Thrmlnra.txt; Thrmnlra/DESIGN.md).
# Our side is on the LEFT, theirs on the RIGHT. The Sarge stands at the far edge of the map.
# 1. Simon says: ARM, LOCK, then TYPE: LAUNCH. No direct order was given. Type it and
#    "WHO TOLD YOU TO LAUNCH?!"; hold off and the machine launches anyway (it heard the
#    Sarge call it). Either way: "NOW LOOK WHAT YOU DID!" and your missiles rise to their
#    pads just above your silos, each with a short name (OWL, ELK, FOX...).
# 2. The recall round: STOP RECALL ALL MISSILES!, then the names, then RECALL THE BOMBERS!
#    (every key moves the bombers toward the first detonation). Each typo alerts one more
#    enemy silo: they do not fire, but it is all your fault now, and it is counted.
# 3. STAND DOWN THE COMMAND: each typo wakes one of OUR silos on the left.
# All the while, "ENTER LAUNCH CODES: _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _" sits on the Big Board, barely
# visible: every mistyped key fills in one letter and the line grows brighter. When it is
# full (or a bomber gets through) the card jumps to Strike.seq. Typed it all before that:
# the Map ends and Peace.seq plays.
# Columns: when | track | clip | settings | what   (see Intro.seq for the words)
when      | track | clip      | settings                                                         | what
0         | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.World; mood=off                                        | a clean map (the Trainer's LAUNCH jump leaves its world behind)
with      | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.World; mood=calm                                       | the globe, subdued, blue bases left, red right, green life between
with      | term  | Console   | x=0.05; y=0.17; w=0.9; rows=4; size=12; clear=yes                | the console at the TOP: eyes stay up on the map
with      | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.Sarge; show=yes; x=0; z=300                            | WIDE: the Sarge at the far edge, fists on hips, facing you
with      | board | Cue       | call=Thrm.Codes                                                  | ENTER LAUNCH CODES: _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _  on the Big Board, upper middle, barely visible
with      | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.Phase; name=recall                                     | from now on a typo alerts an enemy silo and fills a code letter
+0.5      | board | Title     | items=ATTENTION; size=34; y=0.5; color=#FF4040; blink=yes; dur=1.5 | ATTENTION, flashing over the map
+0        | term  | Type      | text=STANDBY FOR FINAL ORDERS. SYSTEM ONLINE.; cps=40             |
+0        | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.Clock; mode=keys                                       | from here the world moves only as you type: every key counts
+0.2      | term  | Drill     | words=ARM,LOCK,LAUNCH; say=TYPE:; trap=yes; trapfire=no; trapwait=6; trapvar=trap; prelaunched={launched}; trappass=GOOD. NO ORDER - NO LAUNCH.; trapfail=WHO TOLD YOU TO LAUNCH?!; alertyell=YOU SEE THAT? THEIR SILO JUST HEARD YOU!,ALERT! THEY HEARD YOU FUMBLE!; good=GOOD.,ADEQUATE.; hold=yes | SIMON SAYS: the Sarge calls LAUNCH without an order. (Typed LAUNCH in the Trainer already: straight to WHO TOLD YOU TO LAUNCH)
+0.3      | term  | Type      | text=LARNCH ORDER ACKNOWLEGDED.; cps=30; color=#C8C8C8            | the machine heard LAUNCH, from you or from the Sarge: it does not know the difference
+0        | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.Raise                                                  | your missiles rise to their pads just above your silos, on the LEFT, names beside them
with      | cam   | Cue       | call=Thrm.CloseUp; dur=2                                         | CLOSE-UP: his angry grid face
with      | term  | Type      | text=NOW LOOK WHAT YOU DID!; cps=40; color=#FFB000                |
+0.2      | term  | Order     | text=STOP RECALL ALL MISSILES!; say=TYPE:; yell=AND THAT WOKE ANOTHER ONE OF THEIR SILOS!,LOOK AT THE MAP. THEY HEARD THAT.; hold=yes | the first order, typed letter for letter
+0.2      | board | Cue       | call=Thrm.Strobe; text=TYPE THE NAME OF THE ASSET TO RECALL      | strobes three times: yellow, orange, RED
with      | term  | Assets    | mode=recall; hold=yes                                            | type OWL, ELK...: each missile sinks back into its silo
+0        | board | Cue       | call=Thrm.Strobe; text=                                          | the strobe goes
+0.2      | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.Bombers                                                | the bombers took off with them: two little triangles crawl right
with      | cam   | Cue       | call=Thrm.CloseUp; dur=2                                         | CLOSE-UP
with      | term  | Type      | text=THE BOMBERS WENT WITH THEM, PRIVATE!; cps=40; color=#FFB000  |
+0.1      | term  | Order     | text=RECALL THE BOMBERS!; call=Thrm.BombersHome; yell=FASTER! THEY ARE NEARLY THERE!,ANOTHER SILO AWAKE. KEEP TYPING!; hold=yes | every key moves the bombers toward the first detonation
+0.3      | term  | Type      | text=YOU STOPPED THE MISSILES. YOU HAVE NOT STOPPED A WAR.; cps=40; color=#FFB000 | the Sarge demands the last one: no war started yet
+0        | world | Cue       | call=Thrm.Phase; name=standdown                                  | now a typo wakes one of OUR silos on the left (and fills a code letter)
with      | term  | Order     | text=STAND DOWN THE COMMAND; yell=THAT ONE WOKE ONE OF OURS!,OUR OWN SILO IS ARMED NOW. WELL DONE.; hold=yes | the last order
+0.3      | term  | Type      | text=COMMAND STANDING DOWN. DISMISSED.; cps=30; color=#FFB000      | the Map ends: Peace.seq (the card)
